 49" style="border:1px solid #789;display:grid;place-items:center;width:22px;height:22px">●</span><span title="Plant 50" style="border:1px solid #789;display:grid;place-items:center;width:22px;height:22px">●</span><span title="Plant 51" style="border:1px solid #789;display:grid;place-items:center;width:22px;height:22px">●</span><span title="Plant 52" style="border:1px solid #789;display:grid;place-items:center;width:22px;height:22px">●</span><span title="Plant 53" style="border:1px solid #789;display:grid;place-items:center;width:22px;height:22px">●</span><span title="Plant 54" style="border:1px solid #789;display:grid;place-items:center;width:22px;height:22px">●</span><span title="Plant 55" style="border:1px solid #789;display:grid;place-items:center;width:22px;height:22px">●</span><span title="Plant 56" style="border:1px solid #789;display:grid;place-items:center;width:22px;height:22px">●</span></div><p>Four feet BETWEEN rows, two feet BETWEEN plants. Six intervals between seven row centers=24ft; seven intervals between eight plant centers=14ft. Total bed edges require extra margin assumptions not specified in source.</p><h2>Original six planting requirements</h2><table class="source-chart" aria-label="Original growing requirements for six source crops"><thead><tr><th>Crop</th><th>Rows apart</th><th>Plants apart</th><th>Yield per plant</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>Strawberries</th><td>4 feet</td><td>2 feet</td><td>12 strawberries/plant</td></tr><tr><th>Cantaloupes</th><td>4 feet</td><td>1 foot</td><td>about 8 cantaloupes/plant</td></tr><tr><th>Zucchini</th><td>5 feet</td><td>1 foot</td><td>about 8 zucchini/plant</td></tr><tr><th>Tomatoes</th><td>4 feet</td><td>2 feet</td><td>about 20 tomatoes/plant</td></tr><tr><th>Pinto beans</th><td>2 feet</td><td>1 foot</td><td>20–25 pods per plant, about 5 beans per pod (100–125 beans per plant)</td></tr><tr><th>Potatoes</th><td>2–3 feet</td><td>1 foot</td><td>5–10 potatoes/plant</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Source assignment:</strong> choose two crops yourself and plan EACH to yield between50 and100, showing number of plants, arrangement and spacing. Example INDEPENDENT Edulytics choice: 6 strawberry plants yield72 and4 tomato plants yield80, provided layout meets source row-spacing rules.</p><p>Teacher assesses diagrams, range assumptions and garden plan; no original Cool-down exists for this optional lesson. Photos inspected but not copied. <a href="https://im.kendallhunt.com/k5/teachers/grade-3/unit-4/lesson-22/lesson.html">2021 teacher source</a>.</p></section>
